description:
We are seeking to expand our Go-To-Market team in RCTT (short for Retail, Consumer, Travel and Transportation) in Europe with a special focus on the Retail sector in the UK&amp;I.&nbsp;

Specifically, we are looking for a leader who is experienced with selling and delivering digital transformations encompassing our core offerings of Customer Experience, Product Innovation, Enterprise Platform Modernization, Data Modernization, AI Readiness, Engineering Excellence and Digital Application and Maintenance Operations (DAMO).&nbsp;

You will be inheriting one large portfolio in the Retail space based on which you will grow the existing account, and acquire new accounts based on your network, your industry expertise and our marketing activities and in close collaboration with your account team, our industry and service line specialists and the RCTT market organization.&nbsp;

As a Client Principals, you are responsible for the entire sales cycle (lead generation through proposal, contract negotiation and closure) as well as client relationship management, account strategy and planning, joint delivery governance and project reviews.&nbsp;

This includes e.g.&nbsp;

● Understand the industry context, the customer problem and define mutual value ● Develop and execute on key account plans and overall go-to-market&nbsp;

● Acquire and nurture senior client relationships on strategic accounts&nbsp;

● Achieve established revenue and profitability targets&nbsp;

● Work closely with the account leadership team (consisting e.g. of the account tech director and account delivery director)&nbsp;

● Actively participate in the go-to-market plan creation/refinement for your account as well as for the industry vertical

About WPP Media

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. With exceptional talent, trusted data and intelligence, and world-class partnerships - all united by our pioneering agentic marketing platform, WPP Open - we help clients navigate change, capture opportunity, and deliver transformational growth. 

WPP Media is WPP's AI-driven media operating unit, bringing together media, data, and partnerships to deliver creative personalisation at scale. Connected through WPP Open and powered by Open Intelligence, clients see exactly where, how, and why their media investment is working.

For more information, visit wppmedia.com .

ROLE SPECIFICATION   &nbsp;

WPP Media Sports &amp; Entertainment    &nbsp;

Job Title: Director, Content Management &nbsp;

Reporting to:    Group Director&nbsp; &nbsp;

Location:  New York&nbsp; &nbsp;

&nbsp;

WPP Media Entertainment   spearheads cutting-edge brand partnerships across entertainment, content and experiential platforms. We are seeking a dynamic entertainment marketing professional to develop and execute high-profile programs that amplify our clients’ brands. The ideal candidate brings proven experience in entertainment and content marketing and the ability to blend creativity, strategic thinking, media expertise and strong project management. This role will be at the forefront of delivering integrated programs across entertainment, IP, publishers, talent and other key industry partners.   &nbsp;

Position Summary &nbsp;

Delivers content strategy and activation across a client portfolio or major account. Provides client counsel, accountability for program and partnership direction, governs quality delivery, and leads teams through high-value engagements. &nbsp;

Responsibilities &nbsp;

• Owns the content agenda and priorities for an assigned major account or portfolio, connecting client objectives to distinctive, audience-relevant content opportunities within the Content Practice vision. &nbsp;

• Leads overall client communications and project management across internal teams ensuring strategic coherence, delivery quality, and a consistent client experience across engagements. &nbsp;

• Informs decisions on partner approach, creative and production direction and issue resolution; elevates decisions within broader practice or enterprise implications. &nbsp;

• Develop brainstorm decks and host internal and client brainstorms based on briefs or proactive opportunities&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Meet and evaluate content &amp; media partners with WPP colleagues to understand the landscape and better inform RFP lists. &nbsp;

• Lead the content strategy and narrative for priority RFPs and proactive recommendations across assigned clients. &nbsp; &nbsp;

• Work with manager to develop RFPs and ensure all information in brief will aid in the best responses from vendors.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Oversee decks and documents creation for client presentations. &nbsp;

• Anticipate market shifts, cultural opportunities, platform changes, and client needs; translate them into recommendations and repeatable approaches for the portfolio. &nbsp;

• Lead and develop Associate Directors and Managers, setting clear expectations, coaching judgment, and reviewing performance. &nbsp;

• Support the Group Director in improving standards, tools, methodologies, talent practices, and the Content Management proposition; contribute portfolio learning, case studies, and points of view. &nbsp;

• Represent assigned portfolio needs and opportunities in capability planning while the Group Director leads capability priorities and the Executive Director retains Content Practice vision, enterprise strategy, and final business decision-making. &nbsp;

